                "entry_id": "d4c984ff-9967-30ac-8fee-7b34ed5ffe49",
                "word": "liberticide",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "bc85f21a-1118-4a15-84e0-f26dad960510",
                        "entry_id": "d4c984ff-9967-30ac-8fee-7b34ed5ffe49",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "liberticides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af2949b9-d9f9-358a-839a-99b7d6eb1e3e",
                        "entry_id": "d4c984ff-9967-30ac-8fee-7b34ed5ffe49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The destruction of liberty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90c74829-75bf-4784-bc29-21a178d16c7f",
                                "sense_id": "af2949b9-d9f9-358a-839a-99b7d6eb1e3e",
                                "text": "All that has been done by the state since the revolt of May is liberticide of the most violent character."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c6ffe41-ec37-4dca-88ad-ace41239a2b2",
                                "sense_id": "af2949b9-d9f9-358a-839a-99b7d6eb1e3e",
                                "text": "In the hands of a designing executive, a standing army was the classic instrument of liberticide."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f0c4182-25b0-4498-8e6d-2a3efa378a3e",
                                "sense_id": "af2949b9-d9f9-358a-839a-99b7d6eb1e3e",
                                "text": "In language and logic we are the prisoners of our premises, just as in politics and law we are prisoners of our rules. Hence we had better pick them well. For if suicide is an illness because it terminates in death, and if the prevention of death by any means necessary is the physician’s therapeutic mandate, then the proper remedy for suicide is liberticide."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13caa044-e831-3535-9f75-bc74abb370e7",
                        "entry_id": "d4c984ff-9967-30ac-8fee-7b34ed5ffe49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who causes the destruction of liberty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99dc03e5-2b82-4e41-9dca-e367d7ec55ec",
                                "sense_id": "13caa044-e831-3535-9f75-bc74abb370e7",
                                "text": "Blind, old, and lonely, when his country's pride, / The priest, the slave, and the liberticide / Trampled and mocked with many a loathed rite / Of lust and blood; he went, unterrified, /"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
